d be no larger than the largest\n    # remaining demand (else it is wasteful fragmentation), and as small\n    # as possible in relative terms.\n    resid_ratio = new_rest / cap\n    largest_remaining = float(np.max(dem))\n    fragmentation = new_rest >= largest_remaining  # leaves unusable slack\n\n    # Prefer non-fragmenting candidates; fall back to all if none exist.\n    if np.any(~fragmentation):\n        mask = ~fragmentation\n    else:\n        mask = np.ones_like(fragmentation, dtype=bool)\n\n    cand_idx = idx[mask]\n    cand_dem = dem[mask]\n    cand_resid = resid_ratio[mask]\n\n    d_cur = dm[current_node][cand_idx] / span\n    d_dep = dm[depot][cand_idx] / span\n\n    # Depot-return alignment: positive when the step moves us toward depot.\n    saving = (d_dep - d_cur) / (d_cur + d_dep + 1e-12)\n\n    # Lexicographic within the band: tightest residual first via a small\n    # weight on residual ratio, then travel + depot-return geometry.\n    score = (1.00 * d_cur\n             - 0.25 * saving\n             + 0.50 * cand_resid)\n\n    return int(cand_idx[np.argmin(score)])","code_sha256":"01ac61889a635b2b73628254e6361c11fba983895dbaad1e34c05e6913543428","elapsed_seconds":0.234,"error_code":null,"error_detail":null,"evaluation_id":"b995c1c52757402e99fec00d362fd2dc","generation_parents":[{"algorithm":"Combine nearest-neighbour travel with a \"savings\" term that rewards customers whose insertion direction aligns with the depot-return vector and penalises residual-capacity fragmentation, scoring candidates by a multi-term geometric priority rather than a pure distance-plus-demand blend.","code_sha256":"815ae10ba19a2037d059bd1256f5814152b390ca0ff8081941759af0c0de740b","population_member_indices":[1],"selected_parent_position":0},{"algorithm":"Scale-normalised blend of current-to-node distance, a depot-return savings ratio, and a capacity-utilisation term that rewards filling the residual load tightly rather than penalising fragmentation.","code_sha256":"3334